<h1>Americas battery market</h1>
<p>North America is a premium, regulation-heavy market; Latin America is import-led with strong two-wheeler and replacement demand.</p>
<h2>What drives the Americas</h2>
<p>The United States is a premium, policy-driven market: tariffs, local-content rules and incentives shape where cells and packs are made. Latin America is an import-led market with strong replacement demand, two-wheeler growth and solar-storage projects. The two halves respond to different signals and should not be averaged into one regional outlook.</p>
<h2>How to read the data</h2>
<p>Separate demand from capacity. A US announcement is not a US factory, and a Latin American import figure is not local production. Check the trade page for HS codes and the demand pages for the segment — automotive, storage or two-wheelers — that matches your product.</p>
<h2>Trade policy</h2>
<p>Tariffs and rules of origin can change the landed cost by more than a factory price move. Confirm the current rate and the origin rule with a broker before quoting a customer, and keep the classification consistent across invoices and shipping documents.</p>

